-- title:
--   Exact pencil: a finite set of Gauss components is realised
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation domain which is henselian as a local ring, with a uniformiser $\varpi$ generating its maximal ideal, let $K_0$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a fraction field of $R$, and let $F$ be a field extension of $K_0$, the $R$-algebra structures being compatible. Let $f \in F$ be transcendental over $R$ and such that $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K_0(f)$ generated by $f$. Let $V$ be a non-empty finite set of valuation subrings of $F$ such that each $O \in V$ contains the image of $R$, has the image of $\varpi$ among its non-units, and satisfies the Gauss condition for $f$: for every $P \in R[X]$ not divisible by $\varpi$, both $P(f)$ and $P(f)^{-1}$ lie in $O$. The conclusion is that there exists $g \in F$, again transcendental over $R$ with $F$ finite-dimensional and separable over $K_0(g)$, such that for every valuation subring $O$ of $F$ containing the image of $R$ and having the image of $\varpi$ as a non-unit, $O$ satisfies the Gauss condition for $g$ if and only if $O \in V$.
--
--   This is a purely valuation-theoretic form of the contraction theorem for normal curves over a henselian discrete valuation ring: the finitely many valuation subrings of $F$ lying over the Gauss point of $f$ play the role of the components of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $f$, and the statement produces a function $g$ whose Gauss components are exactly the prescribed subset $V$. It is used in the construction of normal proper models from prescribed families of valuation subrings, in [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_normalProperModel_of_valuationSubrings_of_form_of_isAlgebraic_relDimOne_genComplete_henselian`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_normalProperModel_of_valuationSubrings_of_form_of_isAlgebraic_relDimOne_genComplete_henselian).
